 Q: Write a SQL query to find all customers who have placed at least one order.

 Query:
 SELECT name
 FROM customers c
 WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1
 FROM orders o
 WHERE o.customer_id = c.customer_id);

 So SELECT 1, SELECT *, or SELECT o.order_id would all work here,
 but SELECT 1 clearly communicates that we only care about existence.


